{"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph stored as adjacency lists: the undirected counterpart of ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"adjacency_list<…, undirectedS>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of unordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"{u, v}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the same edge as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"{v, u}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot (none while the vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order, each its own slot). Edges are kept in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, so an edge’s position in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each slot has a row of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the slots of its neighbors and a parallel row of the positions of its incident edges; each edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is in both its endpoints’ rows, and a self-loop twice in its vertex’s row (as Boost stores it).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The rows share one array per kind, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"many vertices it has. A hash table from unordered slot pair to position (open addressing with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"multiplicative hash, not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Dictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s SipHash) answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in O(1) expected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each edge keeps the orientation it was first inserted with."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/Graph